<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Faisal II of Iraq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1935">1935</a>–<a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Faisal II was the last King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> as a child in 1939, with his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-ilah">Abd al-Ilah</a> as regent until 1953. His governments, dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuri-al-said">Nuri al-Said</a>, were closely tied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad-pact">Baghdad Pact</a>. In February 1958 he formed the Arab Federation with his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">Hussein of Jordan</a>, but on 14 July 1958 army officers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-karim-qasim">Abd al-Karim Qasim</a> overthrew the monarchy and killed him and most of his family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq.jpg" alt="Faisal II of Iraq" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iraqi Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_of_Iraq_-_Faisal_II_1953.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
